# A verification finding is fixed, not argued away

A finding raised by an adversarial verification pass is fixed, not argued away. A real blocker or major
finding from any independent verifier blocks the change, fail-closed, until it is fixed or the maintainer
explicitly reclassifies it with a recorded rationale. A verifier finding may be dismissed as a duplicate
of another only when the dismissal names the kept finding and shows that every line and claim the
dismissed finding cites is covered by the kept one; otherwise the dismissal is refused and the finding
stays open.
